{
  "requirement": "Storage or input resolution errors MUST be reported as errors rather than\ntreated as absent or stale evidence. A callback error MUST NOT be stored as a\ncompleted judgment.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from the requirement text**\n1. Storage errors must be reported as errors, not treated as absent or stale evidence. This covers evidence load, evidence store, and the node-content and edge reads made during the freshness check.\n2. Input resolution errors must be reported as errors. This covers the procedure/version resolver and reads made through the callback context.\n3. A callback error must not be stored as a completed judgment.\n\n**Implementation question.** I read `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph/runtime.rs#impl[Validator<'d, D, F>]/fn[validate_with_edges]` only to find the distinct error paths. There are four. The procedure resolver can fail. `check_with_version` can fail. `graph.validate(&ctx)` can fail. `store_evidence` can fail. Each path propagates its error with `?` before any record is stored.\n\n**Coverage by test**\n- **Procedure/version resolution error.**\n  - `resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments` uses a resolver that returns `Err(\"version\")`.\n  - It asserts `ValidationError::Graph(\"version\")`.\n  - It asserts that no validation was started (`started.is_empty()`).\n- **Evidence load error.** The same test sets `fail_load` and asserts `Err(Graph(\"load\"))`. It is not treated as absent evidence, which would have run the callback.\n- **Evidence store error.** The same test sets `fail_store`. It asserts `Err(Graph(\"store\"))` and that `records` is empty.\n- **Callback error.**\n  - The same test uses `read_in_callback` on an empty graph. This gives `Graph(\"missing\")` and no stored record.\n  - `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` has a callback that asks an agent when none is configured. It asserts `NoAgentConfigured`, `records.is_empty()`, and no reads. It then shows that a correctly configured agent run stores the record normally.\n- **Read and edge errors during the freshness check, with existing evidence.**\n  - `domain_validation_preserves_metadata_reuses_traces_and_propagates_failures` first stores a judgment.\n  - It then sets `fail_read` and `fail_edges` in turn. Each time it asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(failure))`.\n  - It asserts the callback count and write count stay at (1, 1).\n  - It asserts the stored dependencies are unchanged. So the failure was neither treated as stale (which would have re-run and rewritten) nor stored.\n  - It also covers a store failure after the inputs changed. The old stored output is retained, and the next successful call stores the new judgment.\n\n**Assessment.** Every named error class has a test that asserts both that an error is returned and that no judgment is stored or re-run. The error tests carry {test} references to the subject. I found no gap.",
  "references": "3f2764018e0c571f111c3ee1c3c220d17c23bf300b5a5ea841cf63cd776bd341",
